# Append to the END of /etc/ssh/sshd_config on the signer's host (runbook section 5, step 1).
# A Match block lasts to the next Match or the end of the file, so it goes last, not in an
# sshd_config.d include. Check with `sshd -t` and
# `sshd -T -C user=sigvara-tunnel,host=x,addr=72.62.41.138` (and the same for root, unchanged),
# then reload with an admin session kept open.
#
# The tunnel account's key options (restrict,port-forwarding,permitopen=...) re-enable remote
# forwarding too, which would let the key listen on this host's loopback ports. This makes sshd
# itself allow the one local forward to the signer and nothing else.
Match User sigvara-tunnel
    AuthenticationMethods publickey
    AllowTcpForwarding local
    PermitOpen 127.0.0.1:28600
    AllowStreamLocalForwarding no
    PermitTunnel no
    X11Forwarding no
    AllowAgentForwarding no
    PermitTTY no
    PermitUserRC no
    ForceCommand /bin/false
